    "title": "Emma Stone Shimmers in Louis Vuitton on 2026 Oscars Red Carpet",
    "text": "Emma Stone made Sunday night’s 2026 Academy Awards red carpet in Los Angeles her own personal runway in a look by Louis Vuitton. The actress wore a square neck, white shimmering gown with cap sleeves courtesy of the French luxury fashion house. Crafted with elements of iridescent modern luxury and a classic silhouette, the gown offered a formfitting style with a regency-era design. Emma Stone Lexie Moreland The gown’s fabric rendered a liquid-like illusion, and Stone continued her minimalist, yet luxurious, approach with glimmering stud Repossi earrings, framed by her side-parted bobbed hair. You May Also Like Stone’s 2026 awards season has been full of Louis Vuitton designs. A global ambassador and campaign star for the French luxury fashion house since 2017, the actress wore Louis Vuitton to several awards shows leading up to Sunday night’s Oscars. Emma Stone Lexie Moreland Working in collaboration with her stylist, Petra Flannery, Stone’s Louis Vuitton looks have featured colorful displays with simple silhouettes at the Actor Awards on March 1, minimalist glamour at the BAFTAs on Feb. 22 and a rendition of the butter yellow trend at the Golden Globe Awards on Jan. 11. Stone earned her fifth acting Oscar nomination (and second producer nomination) for her work in the Yorgos Lanthimos-directed film “Bugonia.” The actress is a previous recipient of the best Actress in a Leading Role Academy Award for her work in 2016’s “La La Land” and 2023’s “Poor Things.” Emma Stone Lexie Moreland The 2026 Academy Awards honor the best films of 2025 from “One Battle After Another” to “Hamnet” and more. Hosted by Conan O’Brien, who returns for a second consecutive year as master of ceremonies, the awards show takes place at the Dolby Theatre in Los Angeles. “Sinners” leads the night’s nominations, with a record-setting 16 nods including Best Picture. The 2026 Oscars air Sunday night at 7 p.m. ET on ABC and Hulu.",
